{"uid":"e6003ec396201bb6","name":"test_install_survives_an_elevated_euid_workspace_owner_mismatch","fullName":"tests.test_commit_scan_engine_boundary#test_install_survives_an_elevated_euid_workspace_owner_mismatch","historyId":"e0e37b568e79a12ff39cef053af64c41","time":{"start":1791921690487,"stop":1791921690514,"duration":27},"description":"Task cure-01-01-2 (review finding R2, upheld cure-01-02, #210): the\n    real uid boundary runs `install_push_gate` at effective uid 0 (root, via\n    `privsep.root_for_write()`) against a workspace the AGENT uid owns --\n    the exact mismatch git's own \"detected dubious ownership\" safety check\n    (>= 2.35.2) refuses by default, which is why the real container probe\n    (`tests/test_commit_scan_hooks_docker.py`) measured `install_push_gate`\n    returning `None` -- gate not installed -- even though every step up to\n    the `git config core.hooksPath` write had succeeded.\n\n    This sandbox has no real second uid to reproduce the mismatch with a\n    genuinely different file owner, so this pins the DETECTION and its\n    consequences directly: with `os.geteuid()` monkeypatched to a value\n    that differs from the workspace's real owner (exactly the signal\n    `install_push_gate` now reads from the plain filesystem stat, never\n    from `privsep.separated()`), the `git config` call must carry\n    `-c safe.directory=<workspace>` and the install must still succeed --\n    where before this task it would have needed a REAL exception already\n    sitting in `safe.directory` to get this far at all.","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task cure-01-01-2 (review finding R2, upheld cure-01-02, #210): the<br />\nreal uid boundary runs <code>install_push_gate</code> at effective uid 0 (root, via<br />\n<code>privsep.root_for_write()</code>) against a workspace the AGENT uid owns --<br />\nthe exact mismatch git's own &quot;detected dubious ownership&quot; safety check<br />\n(&gt;= 2.35.2) refuses by default, which is why the real container probe<br />\n(<code>tests/test_commit_scan_hooks_docker.py</code>) measured <code>install_push_gate</code><br />\nreturning <code>None</code> -- gate not installed -- even though every step up to<br />\nthe <code>git config core.hooksPath</code> write had succeeded.</p>\n<pre><code>This sandbox has no real second uid to reproduce the mismatch with a\ngenuinely different file owner, so this pins the DETECTION and its\nconsequences directly: with `os.geteuid()` monkeypatched to a value\nthat differs from the workspace's real owner (exactly the signal\n`install_push_gate` now reads from the plain filesystem stat, never\nfrom `privsep.separated()`), the `git config` call must carry\n`-c safe.directory=&lt;workspace&gt;` and the install must still succeed --\nwhere before this task it would have needed a REAL exception already\nsitting in `safe.directory` to get this far at all.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791921690470,"stop":1791921690470,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791921690471,"stop":1791921690477,"duration":6},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_scrub_notifier_env_in_process","time":{"start":1791921690477,"stop":1791921690481,"duration":4},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_task_record_dir","time":{"start":1791921690477,"stop":1791921690477,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"at